akumar and Ramana-Rao conjecture when n is a prime power. ... Akopyan, S. Avvakumov and R. ... Karasev, Equipartition of several measures, http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4762.\n\nNow, we repeat the process of regular convex equipartitions many times, first partitioning the Euclidean space into n_{1} parts, then each part into n_{2} parts, and so on. In this way we obtain iterated convex equipartions of a given convex body into n = n_{1} ⋯ n_{k} parts. Such iterated partitions are parametrised by the (wreath) product of classical configuration spaces. We develop a new configuration space–test map scheme for solving the generalised Nandakumar and Ramana-Rao conjecture using the Hausdorff metric on the space of iterated convex equipartions.\n\nThe new scheme yields a solution to the conjecture if and only if all the n_{i}’s are powers of the same prime. In particular, for the failure of the scheme outside prime power case we give three different proofs.\n\n## Article PDF\n\nArticle PDF\n\nDownload to read the full article text\n\n## References\n\n  1. A. Akopyan, S. Avvakumov and R. Karasev, Convex fair partitions into an arbitrary number of pieces, https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.03057.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA263510 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A263510)\nciteturn5search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.0 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Adjacent sequences: A263507 A263508 A263509 * A263511 A263512 A263513\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquipartition of a Segment | Mathematics of Operations Research (https://doi.org/10.1287%2Fmoor.2022.1260)\nciteturn5search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago;   * [1] Akopyan A, Avvakumov S, Karasev R (2018) Convex fair partitions into an arbitrary number of pieces. ...   * [13] Nandakumar R, Ramana Rao N (2008) ‘Fair’ partitions of polygons—an introduction. ... Sergey Avvakumov, Roman Karasev (2022) Equip